  "title": "Steven S NDE 3370",
  "date": "12/8/05",
  "content": "The third strike of the club put me down to the floor almost instantly. I felt no fear no pain it felt really comfortable not breathing. I felt safe and protected and like I wanted to stay in this state of euphoria. Then a dark space drew me in. Straight after that, I was drawn in to a really bright light where it seemed my whole life flashed by in clips. I mean everything, in seconds. After seeing this, I didn't want to stay here any more. (However comfortable it was.) It felt like I had something I had to come back and do, something to live for, it also felt that something didn't want me to pass over yet. At that point, I heard a voice, I don't know whose it was, unfamiliar, it said calmly, 'You can either stay down and die or stand up and live.' I was given a choice. I took my choice to stand up and live and then felt someone pull my arm through all this. I was completely paralyzed until I felt the pull on my arm. Then I regained mobility and stood up for some reason during all this I was aware of my surroundings.",
